<title>AUSTRALIA: TENNIS-SPAIN BEAT AUSTRALIA 3-2 IN FED CUP PLAY-OFF.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-SPAIN BEAT AUSTRALIA 3-2 IN FED CUP PLAY-OFF.</headline>
<dateline>GOLD COAST, Australia 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain completed a 3-2 win over Australia in their Fed Cup world group play-off on Sunday when they won both the reverse singles and lost the doubles.</p>
<p>Results (Spanish names first):</p>
<p>Arantxa Sanchez Vicario beat Annabel Ellwood 6-2 6-0</p>
<p>Maria Luisa Serna beat Rachel McQuillan 6-1 6-3</p>
<p>Cristina Torrens-Valero/Maria Antonia Sanchez Lorenzo lost to Kerry-Anne Guse/Kristine Kunce 2-6 4-6</p>
<p>Played on Saturday:</p>
<p>Sanchez Vicario beat McQuillan 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>Serna lost to Ellwood 4-6 2-6</p>
</text>
